diff --git a/src/fyd/edge/README.md b/src/fyd/edge/README.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..e653615
--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/fyd/edge/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,91 @@
+# FYD Edge-Object Experience (EDGE-1)
+
+AN OBJECT IS NOT A CARD. AN OBJECT IS A NODE WITH EDGES.
+
+## Invariant
+
+**AN EDGE OBJECT IS NOT SUCCESSFULLY RENDERED UNTIL IT PROVIDES A
+FUNCTIONAL DOORWAY INTO THE AUTHORIZED BUSINESS GRAPH.**
+
+Every edge item maps to a real object id: EDGE ITEM -> OBJECT ID ->
+OBJECT TYPE -> RELATIONSHIPS -> EVIDENCE -> VISIBILITY -> CAPABILITIES ->
+EXPANDED PROJECTION. No decorative images, no presentation-only
+pseudo-objects, no hardcoded business cards, no business-name
+conditionals. The same code renders Happy Place and Coppersmith; only
+the graph data differs.
+
+## Interaction contract (mobile defines it, 375x812)
+
+```
+OBJECT -> TAP -> EXPAND -> EDGES APPEAR -> TRAVERSE EDGE -> NEXT OBJECT -> EXPAND/ACT/ASK/RETURN
+```
+
+- FIRST TAP on any `[data-fyd-object-id]` (service card, margin circle)
+  opens the compact object sheet: identity/title, type, evidence-backed
+  summary, PRIMARY EDGES, capability-resolved actions.
+- SECOND TAP on an edge target traverses to that object's sheet.
+- BACK returns to the previous graph position. Scroll position is
+  preserved; the page is never destroyed; there are no dead-end pages.
+- Desktop: the sheet docks as a side panel. No hover-only paths anywhere.
+
+## Module map
+
+- `types.ts` — ObjectSheet, EdgeGroup, EdgeTargetItem, SheetAction,
+  ClaimClass, and the invariant constant.
+- `resolve.ts` — pure sheet builder. Visibility goes through
+  `filterGraphForViewer` (FYD-010) FIRST; invisible -> null -> HTTP 404,
+  indistinguishable from "unknown". Edge kinds resolve from
+  (predicate, target schema role); unknown predicates fall through to
+  `generic_edge`. Actions resolve through the EXISTING capability path
+  (`capabilityOptions` in `sitespec/schemas.ts` intersected with the ask
+  lane's `VISITOR_ALLOWED_CAPABILITIES`): only actions that exist render.
+  `request_quote` is not a capability in this tree, so no Request-quote
+  button is rendered. Every claim is classified DIRECT_FACT /
+  DERIVED_FACT / OWNER_AUTHORED / GENERATED_COPY; generated copy never
+  masquerades as direct fact.
+- `client.ts` — `edgeClientScript(siteSlug, demoOwner)`: vanilla JS for
+  tap-to-expand, sheet render, traversal stack, Ask FYD with object
+  context (`POST /api/ask` now accepts `objectId`), [Why this?] object
+  and per-edge-group provenance, Open full node, Copy reference.
+- `__tests__/resolve.test.ts` — 20 unit tests over both fixture graphs.
+- `__tests__/q2-hostile.test.ts` — FYD-Q2: HIDE the address, then attack
+  via business edge, Ask FYD, search, related-object traversal, and the
+  why-this gate. Zero public disclosure on every attempt; the demo-owner
+  control proves hiding is a visibility policy, not deletion of the fact.
+
+## Server surface (server/dev-server.ts)
+
+- `GET /api/edge/object?site=&objectId=` -> ObjectSheet JSON (visitor or
+  demo-owner viewer). Hidden/unknown -> 404 `{found:false}`.
+- `POST /api/ask` accepts optional `objectId`: Ask FYD follows the same
+  edges the sheet shows (current object + authorized neighborhood +
+  bound evidence). Humans and agents traverse the same graph.
+- `GET /api/why-this` now checks `canSee` before traversing: the route
+  is the consumer and must gate, per FYD-010.
+
+## Attention model
+
+`EDGE_ATTENTION_LIMIT = 8`: the client renders 8 edge items per group,
+then "Show N more" reveals 8 more. The payload carries every authorized
+item so progressive disclosure never invents objects. The graph may hold
+100 objects; the edge never shows 100 at once.
+
+## Address decision (locked)
+
+The pipeline does NOT own whether a business publishes its address.
+OBSERVED VALUE != PUBLICATION DECISION. Fact, visibility policy, and
+owner override stay separate. A conservative initial visibility is a
+policy, never a deletion of the fact.
+
+## No claim authority (locked)
+
+This module creates no claims and no ClaimAuthority. Render projection
+emits only factual bindings whose provenance resolves to graph/evidence
+or explicit owner-authored content.
+
+## What this lane does NOT own
+
+Graph visualization, a graph database, RelationshipAuthority, another
+canonical store, customer-specific edge components, protocol/federation/
+campaign work. The Ask FYD pipeline and the privacy mask are consumed,
+not rebuilt; the D-IMPL sister lane owns the mask's evolution.
